<div class="doc">
  <p class="eyebrow">SUI</p>
  <h1>The reactive component framework</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    SUI compiles <code>.sui</code> files ahead-of-time into standard web
    components. Signals for reactivity, a strict lint for the design system, and
    output you can drop into any page — no virtual DOM, no framework runtime tax.
  </p>

  <h2>What makes it SUI</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Compiler-first</strong> — templates lower to direct DOM operations; the output is a plain custom element.</li>
    <li><strong>Signals</strong> — fine-grained reactivity; only the readers of a changed signal re-run, no diffing.</li>
    <li><strong>One file</strong> — a <code>.sui</code> holds the markup + bindings and, when there's state, an inline <code>&lt;controller&gt;</code> block (state + logic). Single-file components.</li>
    <li><strong>Strict by design</strong> — the lint turns design-system violations into build errors, so on-brand is the default.</li>
  </ul>

